Helper ownership and concurrency
R3OwnedScriptedPeer is a final checked-Sendable type with immutable listener/origin and Mutex-protected mutable state. The operation closure is @Sendable. Acceptor and handler threads use userInitiated QoS; no blocking accept/read runs in cooperative tasks. QoS is a scheduler request, not a latency guarantee. Worker count increments under the mutex before thread startup, preventing stop from observing a registered-but-not-yet-started worker as complete. close publishes closing before draining connections and closing the listener. An accepted connection arriving later is refused and explicitly closed; acceptFinished is published only after the accept loop's final work. Each worker retains the helper/socket, records errors before decrementing its count, and publishes completion in its final defer. Stop observes acceptFinished && workers==0, meaning final work publication, not physical thread exit or deallocation.
Sockets deliberately remain retained after successful script completion so silent-peer tests do not accidentally turn into EOF tests. Timeline/errors are capped64/8; phase strings are finite at these fixed callsites. Repeated close is idempotent for this usage. stopAndObserve may return false on its2s observation bound or task cancellation; callers expose false in assertions or thrown diagnostics, rather than silently promoting it to completion. Apart from FIXTURE17-01, normal paths and inner caught-error paths invoke this observation.

